# E-learning Lesson
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: E-learning — one unit of a Course's curriculum, unlocked in sequence
# Case 21 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
# References: elearning-course.menata
#
# Split out from elearning-course.menata (corrected 2026-07-11): originally an inline
# `Table of (...)` field. Already fully expressible as an ordinary Object References
# pattern (001-object.md §Relationships) — "a Course has many Lessons" is implied by
# "each Lesson references one Course," no separate grammar needed. Sequence still
# drives the sequential-unlock guard described in elearning-course.menata's header
# (reusing CAP-E06's state-guard shape).

Lesson

Fields

- Course : Course
- Lesson Title : Text
- Content : Rich Text
- Sequence : Number

Constraints

- Lesson Title is required.
- Sequence is required.

Permissions

Instructor

- Author

Student

- View

Views

- Lesson List : List
- Lesson Detail : Detail
